 To have Claude Code, Codex, or another agent CLI install Hive for you (with OS detection, channel selection, Apache Hive collision handling, and `hive init` follow-up), paste the prompt at [install.md](install.md) into the agent. It's the canonical source for agent-driven install — keep it pinned in your agent's context if you reinstall often.
 
+### Local web UI (non-Docker)
+
+Docker/hivebox is one runtime story; local mode is the other, co-equal path. After installing the CLI by any channel above:
+
+```bash
+cd ~/Dev/your-project
+hive setup
+```
+
+One command audits every dependency (auto-bootstrapping Hive-owned ones like qmd and the web bundle; never silently installing/authenticating external CLIs), ensures the daemon runs with the **same binary and version** as your CLI — repairing `/usr/bin/hive`-style drift and stale upgrades — enrolls the project, and points you at `http://127.0.0.1:4567`. Foreground `hive web` always works standalone; `hive web install/start/stop/status/uninstall` manage an optional per-user service (separate from the daemon unit). Loopback binds need no auth; non-loopback binds are refused without `--unsafe-bind`. Full guide: [docs/local-install.md](docs/local-install.md).
