@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+# Local install/run mode (non-Docker)
+
+Local mode is a first-class install/run path for the Hive web UI alongside
+Docker/hivebox (which is unchanged by this mode). One command brings up the
+web UI on your machine, guarantees the daemon is running with the *same*
+Hive binary and version as your CLI, enrolls your project, and gives you a
+bidirectional TUI ⇄ web workflow with no sandboxed data dir — everything
+reads/writes the same XDG/Hive state.
+
+```bash
+cd ~/Dev/your-project   # any git repo you want to drive with Hive
+hive setup
+```
+
+When it converges, `http://127.0.0.1:4567` serves the web UI, tasks created
+in the TUI appear in web immediately (and vice versa), and dispatch runs
+automatically. Windows is out of scope for local web mode; use Docker/hivebox.
+
+## What `hive setup` does
+
+| Step | Detail |
+|---|---|
+| 1. Dependency audit | Ruby ≥ 3.4, git, tmux, gh (installed **and** authenticated), claude, codex, Node/npm, qmd, Rails web bundle |
+| 2. Bootstrap Hive-owned gaps | qmd (`npm install --global --prefix <hive data>/qmd @tobilu/qmd`) and the web bundle (`bundle install`) are auto-installed. External CLIs are **never** installed or authenticated silently — their exact fix command is printed verbatim instead |
+| 3. Daemon guarantee | The daemon service must run with the SAME binary + version as this CLI. Path drift (`/usr/bin/hive` from an old package), stale versions, stopped-but-registered services: detected and repaired (unit rewritten against the current binary, restarted through systemd-user/launchd) |
+| 4. Enrollment | `hive init .` semantics; already-initialized projects are reported as enrolled, not re-scaffolded |
+| 5. Web launch | Default prints the foreground hint (`hive web`). `--managed` installs + starts the `hive-web` user service instead; `--no-web` skips |
+
+Exit codes: `0` converged; `65` at least one dispatch-critical dependency
+(`claude`/`codex`/`gh`) still failing — the web UI may already be up, but
+dispatch needs those fixed first.
+
+Flags:
+
+```
+--project DIR   enroll this directory (default: cwd)
+--managed       install + start the managed hive-web service
+--no-web        skip web bring-up entirely
+--yes           non-interactive
+```
+
+Re-running `hive setup` on a converged machine is a fast no-op pass.
+
+## Foreground vs managed web
+
+Foreground is always the zero-config default:
+
+```bash
+hive web                 # http://127.0.0.1:4567, Ctrl-C to stop
+```
+
+Optional managed service — a SEPARATE unit from the daemon, never merged:
+
+```bash
+hive web install         # writes ~/.config/systemd/user/hive-web.service (Linux)
+                         # or ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.hive-web.plist (macOS)
+hive web start           # systemctl --user start hive-web / launchctl load …
+hive web status          # running/stopped + bound URL (exit 1 when stopped)
+hive web stop
+hive web uninstall
+```
+
+The generated unit pins the absolute resolved path of the installing `hive`
+binary and bakes your resolved bind/port plus HOME/XDG paths, so the served
+app reads exactly the same config/state as an interactive TUI run.
+
+## Bind/auth policy
+
+* Loopback binds (`127.0.0.1`, `::1`, `localhost`) need no auth — single-user
+  local mode.
+* Non-loopback binds are REFUSED unless `web.origin` starts with `https://`
+  (implying a trusted fronting proxy) or you pass `--unsafe-bind`. The flag
+  is never persisted: every unsafe start must re-affirm it.
+* Port already taken → actionable error naming the listener when visible,
+  suggesting `--port`.
+
+The Docker/hivebox container keeps its own documented posture: inside the
+container supervisor, `--bind 0.0.0.0` keeps the legacy warn-only behavior.
+
+## Dependency reference
+
+| Dependency | Kind | On failure |
+|---|---|---|
+| Ruby ≥ 3.4 | external | fix command printed |
+| git, tmux, node, npm | external | fix commands printed |
+| gh | external, critical | `gh auth login` printed; never auto-run |
+| claude, codex | external, critical | presence + credential-artifact probe; exact remediation printed |
+| qmd | Hive-owned | auto-bootstrapped into `<data>/hive/qmd` |
+| Rails web bundle | Hive-owned | `bundle install` against the lockfile |
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+Run `hive setup` again — its summary table lists every check with status and
+the verbatim fix command. Common findings:
+
+* `daemon path_mismatch: unit pins "/usr/bin/hive"` — another hive install's
+  service is registered. Repair with `hive daemon install --force` (or let
+  `hive setup` do it).
+* `stale daemon: unit binary reports v0.x but CLI is v0.y` — restart via
+  repair; the running process predates your upgrade.
+* `gh unauthenticated` — run `gh auth login`.
+* Web won't start: check `hive web` foreground output first; port conflicts
+  name the holder.
