@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+---
+title: Hive::Local
+type: module
+source: lib/hive/local/
+created: 2026-08-25
+updated: 2026-08-25
+tags: [module, local, setup, web, daemon, drift]
+---
+
+**TLDR**: The first-class LOCAL (non-Docker) install/run mode
+(`hive setup`, hardened foreground `hive web`, managed `hive web
+install|start|stop|status|uninstall`, daemon binary-consistency guarantee).
+Shared check engine under `Hive::Local::*`; Docker/hivebox is unaffected.
+
+## Module map
+
+| Module | File | Purpose |
+|--------|------|---------|
+| `Hive::Local::DependencyAudit` | `lib/hive/local/dependency_audit.rb` | One audit engine for every dependency (Ruby ≥ 3.4, git, tmux, gh+auth, claude+auth, codex+auth, node/npm, qmd, web bundle). Classifies rows as `ok` / `missing` / `wrong_version` / `unauthenticated` / `unavailable`; hive-owned rows (`qmd`, `web-bundle`) carry a bootstrap command setup may run — externals are diagnose-only with verbatim fix commands. Pure classifier (`classify`) is unit-tested without spawning. |
+| `Hive::Local::DaemonDriftCheck` | `lib/hive/local/daemon_drift.rb` | Binary/version consistency between the invoking CLI (`Hive::InvokedBinary.path`, `Hive::VERSION`) and the installed daemon service unit (systemd `ExecStart=` first shellword / launchd ProgramArguments 4th string). Statuses: `ok` / `not_installed` / `not_running` / `path_mismatch` / `version_mismatch`. `repair!` force-reinstalls the unit against the current binary and restarts through the service manager — including an EXPLICIT restart when a version-only drift renders byte-identical unit content (`:unchanged`). Exposes an audit-shaped row via `check`. |
+| `Hive::Commands::Setup` | `lib/hive/commands/setup.rb` | `hive setup` orchestrator: audit → bootstrap hive-owned failures → ensure daemon (install if absent / repair if drifted / enable --now if stopped) → idempotent enrollment (`hive init .` semantics) → web launch hint or `--managed` service → summary table. Exit 65 when dispatch-critical externals still fail; never silently installs/authenticates them. |
+| `Hive::Web::BindPolicy` | `lib/hive/web/bind_policy.rb` | Bind/auth gate for the local web tier: loopback = no auth by default; non-loopback refused unless an https origin implies a fronting proxy or `--unsafe-bind` re-affirms per run (never persisted). Inside the hivebox supervisor (`HIVEBOX_SUPERVISOR_PID` present) the legacy warn-only posture applies so the container path is unaffected. |
+| `Hive::Commands::Web` (extended) | `lib/hive/commands/web.rb` | Foreground default unchanged (loopback `127.0.0.1:<web.port>`), now gated by BindPolicy with a pre-exec port-in-use probe naming the listener. New subcommands `install/start/stop/status/uninstall` manage the web service lifecycle. |
+| `Web::ServiceInstaller` | `lib/hive/commands/web/service_installer.rb` | Per-user managed-service installer for the web tier over the shared `ServiceInstaller::Base` mechanics. SEPARATE identity from the daemon (`hive-web.service` / `local.hive-web` — merging is forbidden). Pins absolute binary + resolved bind/port and bakes HOME/XDG_* absolute values so the served app resolves the same state as the TUI ("works in terminal, broken as a service" guard). |
+
+## Wiring
+
+```
+hive setup
+  ├─ DependencyAudit.audit ── bootstrap!(hive-owned only) ── re-probe
+  ├─ DaemonDriftCheck.call ── repair! (not_installed/drifted)
+  │                          └─ enable --now (not_running)
+  ├─ Init.new(project).call (idempotent enrollment)
+  ├─ Web::ServiceInstaller.install!/start! (--managed)
+  └─ summary table (+ exit 65 on critical externals)
+
+web UI ⇄ daemon health
+  GET  /health/daemon         DaemonDriftCheck.call (login-required)
+  POST /health/daemon/repair  DaemonDriftCheck.repair!
+```
+
+## Trust boundaries
+
+* External agent CLIs are NEVER installed or authenticated by the audit,
+  setup, or web surfaces — remediation commands are emitted verbatim.
+* Non-loopback web binds without auth require the explicit per-run
+  `--unsafe-bind` flag.
+* The browser repair endpoint requires login (standard Rails CSRF applies);
+  unauthenticated deployments get no repair surface.
